======================================================================
  OVERALL FINDINGS TABLE
======================================================================
  saved table: Table_FINDINGS_overall_v9.csv
  - H2 cash flow by super-group: Negative in all 6 groups; significant at 5% in 4/6, at 10% in 6/6.
      => Most universal result — consistent negative sign everywhere, strongest of the four.
  - H1 margin by super-group: Significant at 5% only in: Healthcare (a FRAGILE group); Retail borderline (p=0.05).
      => Per-group H1 is weak and rests on a fragile group; the pooled H1 result is the reportable one, not the group decomposition.
  - Distress by super-group: Significant in only some groups at the per-group level.
      => Pooled result stronger than any single group (per-group power limited).
  - Returns by super-group: Group-fragile; some groups show wrong-sign spreads.
      => Pooled is primary; per-group decomposition shows where signal is detectable.
  - Fragile groups: S4 Technology (29f, 79% US) and S6 Healthcare (21f, 71% US).
      => Flag everywhere; do not build narrative on their per-group estimates.
  - US-share by group: Ranges 51-79%; tech & healthcare most US-heavy.
      => Per-group claims for US-heavy groups are effectively US claims.

